<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What is a case packing conveyor system?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>A case packing conveyor system integrates case erectors, product collating conveyors, case packers, case sealers, and case transport conveyors into a unified end-of-line system. The conveyor connects each machine and buffers product between operations.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">Drop-pack vs. wrap-around case packing?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Drop-pack drops product vertically into pre-erected cases, suits rigid bottles and cans. Wrap-around forms the case around the product group, uses less corrugated, fits tighter, but requires stable product. See also: <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/case/robotic-case-packing/">robotic case packing</a>.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What conveyor types connect packer to palletizer?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/live-roller-conveyors/">Belt-driven live roller</a>, <a href="/conveyor-types/cdlr-conveyors/">CDLR</a>, or <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR conveyors</a> carry sealed cases to the palletizer, with accumulation zones for palletizer staging. Size capacity and speed from your heaviest case and the packer rate.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-4">How fast do case packing lines run?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-4" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>It depends on packer type, products per case, and case size. Manual-assist stations run at operator pace. Automatic and robotic packers run faster, and multi-robot cells add rate. Wexxar rates its WF30 fully automatic case erector at up to 30 CPM. The conveyor system must match packer output while providing accumulation for downstream equipment.</p>

</div>
</div>
